### Depot-Site Routes API Tests
### Demonstrates soft-delete recovery functionality

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
@token = your-jwt-token-here

### 1. Login to get JWT token (replace with actual credentials)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "password"
}

### 2. Create a new depot-site route
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/user/depot-sites
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "depotId": 1,
  "siteId": 1,
  "distanceKm": 15.5,
  "travelTimeMins": 25,
  "returnTimeMins": 20,
  "active": true,
  "isPrimary": true,
  "transportRate": 2.50
}

### 3. Get all routes (should show the created route)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/depot-sites
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Get the specific route by ID (replace {id} with actual ID from step 2)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/depot-sites/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Delete the route (soft delete)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/user/depot-sites/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Get all routes again (route should be gone from list)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/depot-sites
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Try to get the deleted route by ID (should return 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/depot-sites/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. SMART RECOVERY TEST: Create the same depot-site combination again
### This should reactivate the soft-deleted route with new data
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/user/depot-sites
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "depotId": 1,
  "siteId": 1,
  "distanceKm": 18.0,
  "travelTimeMins": 30,
  "returnTimeMins": 25,
  "active": true,
  "isPrimary": false,
  "transportRate": 3.00
}

### 9. Get all routes (should show the reactivated route with new data)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/depot-sites
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Get the route by ID (should show the same ID as step 4, but with new data)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/depot-sites/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11. Verify the route has been reactivated with new values
### The response should show:
### - Same ID as before (proving it's the same record)
### - deletedAt: null (proving it's been reactivated)
### - Updated values (distanceKm: 18.0, travelTimeMins: 30, etc.)
### - Updated timestamp

### Additional Tests

### 12. Test creating a route that already exists (should fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/user/depot-sites
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "depotId": 1,
  "siteId": 1,
  "distanceKm": 20.0,
  "travelTimeMins": 35,
  "active": true
}

### 13. Get routes by depot
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/depot-sites/depot/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 14. Get routes by site
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/depot-sites/site/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 15. Get only active routes
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/depot-sites/active
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 16. Get only primary routes
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/depot-sites/primary
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 17. Search routes
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/depot-sites/search?query=depot
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 18. Set primary depot for a site
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/user/depot-sites/site/1/primary-depot/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 19. Update a route
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/user/depot-sites/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "distanceKm": 16.5,
  "travelTimeMins": 28,
  "active": false
}

### 20. Check if route exists
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/depot-sites/1/exists
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Expected Behavior Summary:
### 1. Create route ? Route created with ID 1
### 2. Delete route ? Route soft-deleted (deletedAt set)
### 3. Recreate same depot-site ? Existing route reactivated (deletedAt = null)
### 4. Same ID returned ? Proves it's the same database record
### 5. New data applied ? All fields updated with new values
### 6. No duplicate error ? Smart recovery prevents constraint violations